          %title
          %p
            This is a timeline of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            and related mathematics.
          %h1#timeline Timeline
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th Year
                %th
                %th Contributors
                %th
                %th Event
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1848
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  Arthur Cayley
                  %sup
                    %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Timeline+of+category+theory+and+related+mathematics#1"} [1]
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Computations with complexes, Koszul resolutions, notion of exactness; main result: the resultant is a determinant of a Koszul complex.
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1890
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Hilbert"} David Hilbert
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    resolution
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/resolution+of+modules"} ?
                  and free resolution of modules
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1890
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Hilbert"} David Hilbert
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    Hilbert syzygy theorem
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Hilbert+syzygy+theorem"} ?
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1893
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Hilbert"} David Hilbert
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nullstellensatz"} fundamental theorem of algebraic geometry
                  also called Hilbert Nullstellensatz. It was later reformulated to: the category of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+variety"} affine varieties
                  over a field
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  is equivalent to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} dual
                  of the category of reduced finitely generated (commutative)
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+unital+algebra"} algebras
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1894
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Poincar%C3%A9"} Henri Poincaré
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1895
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Poincar%C3%A9"} Henri Poincaré
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homology"} simplicial homology
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1895
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Henri+Poincar%C3%A9"} Henri Poincaré
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  fundamental work
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Analysis+Situs"} Analysis Situs
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1923
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    Otto Künneth
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Otto+K%C3%BCnneth"} ?
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kunneth+formula"} Künneth formula
                  for (co)homology of product of spaces
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1926
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Otto+Schreier"} Otto Schreier
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Classifies nonabelian extensions of groups having implicitly notions of a pseudofunctor and nonabelian cohomology in dimensions up to 3
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1929
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    Walther Mayer
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Walther+Mayer"} ?
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1930
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ernst+Zermelo"}> Ernst Zermelo
                  –
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abraham+Fraenkel"} Abraham Fraenkel
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  Statement of the final
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZF-axioms
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
                  after being first stated in 1908 and improved upon since then
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1932
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} [Georges de Rham]
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} de Rham theorem: For a smooth manifold the de Rham cohomology is isomorphic to the singular cohomology with coefficients in R.
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1932
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eduard+%C4%8Cech"} Eduard Čech
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C4%8Cech+cohomology"}> Čech cohomology
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} higher homotopy groups
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                  though nobody paid attention because they were all abelian.
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1933
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Solomon+Lefschetz"} Solomon Lefschetz
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1934
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reinhold+Baer"} Reinhold Baer
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Ext groups, Ext functor (for abelian groups and with different notation)
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1935
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witold+Hurewicz"} Witold Hurewicz
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} higher homotopy groups
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1936
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marshall+Stone"} Marshall Stone
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  Stone representation theorem for Boolean algebras initiates various
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+duality"} Stone dualities
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1937
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
