              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1978
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Don Anderson
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  Building on work of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Brown"} Kenneth Brown
                  defines
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    ABC (co)fibration categories
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/ABC+categories"} ?
                  for doing homotopy theory and more general
                  = succeed "," do
                    %span.newWikiWord
                      ABC model categories
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/new/ABC+model+category"} ?
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} Quillen model category
                  is an ABC model category. A difference to Quillen model categories is that in ABC model categories fibrations and cofibrations are independent and that for an ABC model category M
                  %sup D
                  is an ABC model category. To a ABC (co)fibration category is canonically associated a (left) right
                  = succeed "." do
                    %span.newWikiWord
                      Heller derivator
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Derivator"} ?
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+model+structure"} Hurewicz model structure
                  on Top. Complexes of objects in an abelian category with quasi-isomorphisms as weak equivalences and monomorphisms as cofibrations form an ABC precofibration category
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1978-1979
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  Alexander Beilinson
                  %sup
                    %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Timeline+of+category+theory+and+related+mathematics"} [3]
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Two articles on the structures of derived categories of coherent sheaves on projective spaces, which started a rich theory of relations between linear algebra of quivers and triangulated categories coming from algebraic geometry. This is continued in 1979 a famous related article of Bernstein-Gel’fand-Gel’fand with importance to physics and representation theory.
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1979
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Don Anderson
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
